(LST2-71 — `respectively` is described as reserved as a possible future
 zip marker and "not parsed today". The second half is true: a sentence
 using it does not compile. The first half is not: `respectively` is
 accepted as an ordinary variable name. See Discrepancy 9.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-71.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   4
   a zip marker sentence does not compile: see D9.vox
)
a number called respectively is 4.
print respectively.
print "a zip marker sentence does not compile: see D9.vox".
